Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 32 CLINICAL DATA  69 year old women with left breast carcinoma  Long lateral suture  short superior                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  EXTENSIVE  EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  2  MAMMARY CARCINOMA IN SITU  SMALL FOCI  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Infiltrating carcinoma involves many areas of the excision specimen  The foci of in situ carcinoma are small and distinction of lobular from ductal type is difficult  No definite vascular invasion is identified  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY CONTENTS   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 11 OF 11 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Daniel Rubin  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 07 49 Proofread by  RUBIN DANIEL                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 