 Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 11 50 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm lymph node bisected and entirely frozen as FX 1  resubmitted in cassette A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with attached axillary contents  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm ellipse contains a firm nipple with a bluish discoloration  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm hard  gritty blue dyed stellate mass immediately subjacent to the nipple  The mass is 3 6cm from the deep margin and 3 5cm from the inferior margin  and it does not grossly involve the skin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  The axillary contents are dissected to reveal multiple lymph nodes ranging in size from 0 5cm in diameter to 1 5cm in diameter  Section code  B D  representative sections of mass E   margin closest to mass G H J  axillary lymph nodes entirely submitted  K N  additional sections of mass  with closest inferior margin in M  O   closest deep margin  Resident  GUILLERMO J TEARNEY  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODE  LEFT SENTINEL   POSITIVE FOR METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA CONSISTENT WITH BREAST ORIGIN  O R  Resident  SONER ALTIOK  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  LYMPH NO