  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  breast tissue calcification  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm unoriented fibroadipose breast tissue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal fibrous breast parenchyma  submitted entirely in A through F  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  breast nodule  is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 0 6cm fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  Submitted entirely in G and H  Resident  GUILLERMO J TEARNEY  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   RIGHT BREAST   NO AREAS SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  GROSS DIAGNOSIS   RIGHT BREAST NODULE   NO AREAS SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  ZUOQIN TANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  ESTHER OLIVA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  TISSUE CALCIFICATIONS    EXCISIONAL PART B  BREAST  RIGHT  BREAST NODULE    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
