ve result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 08 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm breast tissue with short stitch posteriorly  2 pins  long stitch   1 pin  laterally  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 5cm ill defined tan white  firm mass that abuts the lateral margin  Representative section of tumor at the closest  lateral  margin is frozen as FX 1 and the is submitted in cassette A  The extreme posterior margin is submitted in cassette B and the next adjacent section is submitted in cassette C  The posterior margin is double inked with green color and the anterior margin inked black in cassette C   The tumor closest to the closest margin  lateral  is submitted in cassette D  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  new margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fibrofatty tissue  Long stitch is in the lateral side and the short stitch in the superior side  The old margin is inked in black and the new lateral margin is inked in blue  The superior margin is inked in red  Representative section taken through the old margin and the new margins are presented in cassettes E G  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                              