n this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 21 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast and axillary dissection  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm mastectomy with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm skin ellipse with an unremarkable 1 5cm nipple  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm axillary tail is attached to the main specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm firm  tan white stellate nodule extending to approximately REMOVED_DATE to 0 2cm of the deep resection margin  Further sectioning reveals the remainder of the breast to be composed of predominantly fibrous  tan rubbery tissue intermixed with unremarkable adipose tissue  A representative section of the firm mass and deep resection margin is submitted in cassette A  Representative sections of the remainder of the mass are submitted in cassettes B through E  Representative sections of unremarkable parenchyma are submitted entirely in cassette F  The axillary tail is sectioned to reveal multiple rubbery tan pink lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 2 0cm  The lymph nodes are submitted entirely in cassettes G through M  The nipple is trisected and submitted entirely in cassette N  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  AMBULATORY GEN SURG   ACC 457 REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT  and AXILLARY CONTENTS   report_end  , Unchecked.
