erin negative ductal carcinomas  Other pathologists might classify the carcinomas as having both ductal and lobular features  All the tumor nodules have similar morphologic features  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  2 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm  posterior   REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  anterior   and several additional foci ranging from  0 1cm to 0 3cm  GRADE  2  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Suspicious  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Invasive carcinoma focally extends to 0 18cm from the posterior margin and is  0 2cm from the anterior margin  LOCATION OF THE DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within and beyond the region of the invasive carcinomas  and spanning the tissue between the posterior and anterior invasive tumors  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2 to 3  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends to 0 1cm from the posterior margin of the specimen in several foci and to 0 1cm from the anterior margin in one focus  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Her 2 only   See also  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   SKIN  RIGHT BREAST  MASTECTOMY FLAP   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 3 containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   Glew  REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  right breast sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm portion of soft tan red tissue which is bisected to reveal a smooth tan red cut surface and a well circumscribed tan white area measuring 0 3cm in greatest dimension  The specimen is entirely submitted for frozen section as FX 1  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  right breast   is a 19 x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm right breast simple mastectomy specimen partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm ovoid portion of tan pink skin with a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan pink unremarkable nipple which comes to 0 9cm of the skin margin  A black stitch designates the axillary tail  The anterior margin is inked blue  the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm indurated tan pink nodule in the upper outer quadrant which comes to 0 4cm of the posterior margin and 0 7cm of the anterior margin  This nodule is located within a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm region of firm nodular gray pink mammary tissue which comes to 0 2cm of the posterior margin and 0 4cm of the anterior margin  Located approximately 2 5cm inferomedial and anterior to the nodule is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm cavity consistent with previous biopsy site which contains dark red blood and is surrounded by soft yellow discoloration consistent with fat necrosis  The cavity abuts the anterior margin and comes to 1 0cm of the posterior margin  The cavity is located in the mid outer breast tissue  Along the periphery of the cavity superomedially there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm indurated gray white nodular area which comes to 0 5cm of the anterior margin  The remaining cut surface displays hemorrhage and dense gray white fibrous tissue with no other discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity with posterior margin as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   anterior margin as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and subjacent firm nodule as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue between cavity and upper outer quadrant nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper outer quadrant nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Firm nodular tissue surrounding upper outer quadrant nodule submitted from medial to lateral   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue from upper outer quadrant which may represent lymph nodes  Received in formalin  labeled  right breast tissue mastectomy flap   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm aggregate of unremarkable tan pink skin with a small amount of attached tan red fibrofatty tissue  Representative sections are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT BREAST SENTINEL   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA  Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 28   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 05 02 23PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erbB 2 Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Thursday REMOVED_MONTH 29   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01 12 13PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Lymph Node  Right Axilla  Sentinel   Excision PART B  Breast  Right   Simple 