Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  19 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  19 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 23 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  SPECIMEN  1   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE II III  EXTENDING TO THE ANTERIOR MARGIN  WITH FOCI OF LYMPHATIC INVASION  SEE NOTE   NOTE  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  The carcinoma is a single mass of 2 5cm  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  ASSOCIATED WITH THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  BREAST  LEFT  SPECIMEN  2   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE  2  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 18 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 17 41                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we 