 carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 19 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name  unit number  and  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of oriented breast  The superior resection margin is inked red  the inferior blue  the anterior green  the deep  posterior  inked yellow  and the medial and lateral are inked black  Sectioned to show white plugs extruding from ducts and a focally firm area  approximately 0 5cm in greatest dimension   Submitted entirely in A G  from medial to lateral  with the suspicious lesion in cassette D  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS EXAM  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  SUSPICIOUS LESION  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robin E  Kirby  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Timothy Edward Guiney  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
