ioning with described solid mass  towards medial   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Continued serial sectioning with the superior margin in this cassette   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial margin  en face  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm aggregate of fat  containing two lymph nodes  The smaller lymph node is inked black  Both nodes are bisected and the larger is frozen as FX 1 and submitted now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The smaller lymph node is frozen as FX 1A  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  additional lateral tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 1cm C shaped soft tissue specimen  The surgeon marks the superior end with a short stitch  and the lateral surface with a long stitch  The surgeon confirms that the lateral aspect of the specimen is to be inked  This surface is inked black  On the non inked surface of the specimen  there is white fibrous tissue  The following cassettes are submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Serial sectioning from the superior aspect to the inferior aspect of the specimen    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  contains the most superior part of this specimen  This superior lateral part of the specimen is extensively sampled    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from the mid to inferior aspect of the specimen    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is the most inferior part of the specimen  Approximately 60  of the specimen is submitted   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast final superior  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm dome shaped soft tissue specimen  The new margin as designated by surgeon is inked black  This specimen is serially sectioned to reveal white fibrous tissue  Submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS 