rong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 16 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast lumpectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm portion of breast tissue with localizing wire in place  The accompanying radiograph discloses a discrete mass  There is a short stitch designating superior and long stitch designating lateral aspect  Specimen is blue inked on the lateral aspect  black inked on the medial aspect  Specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm well delineated tan white firm lesion which is within 0 4cm of the inferior margin  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm tan red firm well defined nodule located 0 1cm from the lateral margin  The remaining parenchyma is 90   yellow lobulated fatty tissue and 5  thin white fibrous tissue  Representative sections are submitted sequentially from anterior to posterior as follows  A D  Tumor to inferior margin E  Representative P Q  Second nodule Received in formalin  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  sentinel node  83  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan pink rubbery lymph node which on sectioning reveals a tan pink fatty surface  Specimen is entirely submitted as F R S  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  non sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan red fatty rubbery lymph node which is bisected and submitted entirely as G