e result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 MAY 96 at 16 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm piece of breast with a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating the lateral aspect  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an ill defined stellate  firm mass approximately 1 0cm in greatest dimension  adjacent to the superior medial inked margin  A representative section of this area is frozen as FX 1  and saved frozen  Representative sections of the medial half are submitted from superior to inferior  A through E  and representative sections of the lateral half are submitted superior to inferior in F through J  Labeled   2  right medial  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of breast tissue with short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral  The specimen is inked black and the medial margin is inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely from superior to inferior in K through O  Labeled   3  right superior  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm portion of breast with a long suture designating the lateral  and a short suture designating the superior    anterior  margin  The specimen is inked black and the anterior flat surface    inferior aspect  is designated blue  The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial and submitted in P through S  Labeled  right axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x