protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 06 08     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     Note  The overall histomorphological features  which include focal gland formation  are that of invasive ductal rather than invasive lobular carcinoma  The tumor is graded according to the modified Bloom and Richardson grading method  The tumor is scored 3 for tubule formation  and 2 for nuclear pleomorphism  The mitotic rate  10 high power field  HPF  were examined  is between REMOVED_DATE mitotic figures per HPF  this mitotic rate scores a 2 on the modified Bloom and Richardson scale  Therefore  the total score  combining tubule  nuclear pleomorphism and mitotic rate  is 7  A score of 7 classifies this neoplasm as Grade 2  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 17 33 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  long lateral and short superior  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm spherical piece of breast tissue oriented by a long stitch at the lateral resection margin and a short stitch at the superior resection margin  On palpation  it appears centrally firm and nodular  The resection margins are inked as posterior in black  anterior in blue  superior and inferior in green  lateral in yellow  and medial in orange  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a central  stellate  hard and white tan tumor  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm  located 0 2cm from the mid posterior resection margin which is the closest resection margin  The remaining surrounding breast tissue appears white tan  rubbery  and homogeneous with focal areas of hemorrhage  SECTION CODE A  Tumor and posterior closest resection margin  B  Tumor and anterior superior resection margins  C  Tumor and anterior resection margin  D  Tumor and mid superior resection margin  E  Tumor only  F  Medial portion of tumor  G  Lateral portion of tumor including anterior and inferior margins  H  Portion of tumor including inferior and posterior resection margins  I  Lateral margin  radial  grossly unremarkable  J  Medial margin  radial  grossly unremarkable  Received in saline   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left hard and blue sentinel node   REMOVED_CASE_ID   are two small lymph nodes measuring 0 4cm and 0 7cm in greatest diameter  entirely submitted as K  Received in saline   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  non sentinel lymph nodes  is a 0 6cm in diameter lymph node  with an attached yellow tan unremarkable fatty tissue  The lymph node is submitted as L  Received in saline   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  226 sentinel node  286 pale blue  are three lymph nodes and attached fatty tissue ranging from 0 4cm to 0 6cm in greatest diameter  entirely submitted as M  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  addition inferior deep margin  are two irregular and unoriented pieces of breast and fatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The elongated piece is inked in black and entirely submitted as N  The second piece is sectioned and entirely submitted as O  Received in saline   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margin  are multiple and unoriented pieces of irregular breast fibrous and fatty tissue measuring 