 the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 16 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with sutures designating medial  double pin  and inferior  single pin   This specimen is inked black  the anterior margin double inked with yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a 1 2cm diameter firm area grossly abutting the anterior margin  Representative section of this margin is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remainder of tissue are submitted entirely in cassettes A   M  proceeding laterally to medially  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  leftt breast  additional mass  are several fragments of yellow to pink fibroadipose tissue  one of which is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm with a long stitch marking the medial and short stitch marking the inferior aspect of the specimen  The anterior surface of this particular fragment is more fibrous than the posterior surface  The later consists mostly of yellow adipose tissue  The entire specimen is inked black  the anterior surface is double inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm white firm mass located on the superior aspect of this specimen abutting against both the anterior and posterior resection surfaces  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes N through Q  The other fragments of fibroadipose tissue within the same specimen container are th