Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 50 CLINICAL DATA  Breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM A MARGIN  SLIDE B   THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  2  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  INVOLVING SCATTERED DUCTS AND LOBULES AND PRESENT AT OR VERY NEAR RESECTION MARGINS  3  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SINGLE MICROSCOPIC FOCUS AWAY FROM THE MAIN TUMOR MASS  4  DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA AND LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  5  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  6  SMALL DUCT PAPILLOMA  NOTE  Neither vascular nor lymphatic invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 47 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3cm excisional biopsy of fibrofatty breast tissue which contains REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm tan white firm irregular stellate lesion that approaches the inked resection margin by 0 1cm  The remaining breast tissue contains mature adipose tissue and white rubbery firm tissue  A representative section of the lesion is frozen as frozen section  1  and submitted in A  Section Code  A  frozen section  1  B G  mass and adjacent resection margin  H N  grossly uninvolved parenchyma and inked margins  80  of the specimen is submitted  Resident  Rex Neal Smith  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST RIGHT  EXCISIONAL  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
