rformance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  23 MAY 02 at 10 23 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast  is a 12 x 11 x 4cm oriented portion breast tissue with a long stitch designating lateral and a short stitch designating anterior  The specimen is inked as follows  posterior black  anterior blue  medial stripe of red  lateral stripe of orange  Sectioning of the specimen reveals a poorly defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fibrous area in the middle of the specimen  It is approximately 1 4cm to the closest anterior resection margin and more than 2 5cm from the other resection margins  No gross abnormalities are identified in the remaining specimen  Representative sections are submitted  A D  Lesion entirely submitted from medial to lateral E F  Two sections taken from area adjacent to lesion G H  Two sections far away from the lesion Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  axilla  left breast  is a 13 x 11 x 2cm portion of fibrofatty tissue with multiple lymph nodes  ranging from 0 3cm to 3 5cm in largest dimension  are identified  No other gross abnormalities are seen  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted  SECTION CODE I N  One bisected lymph node in each O Q  Lymph nodes R T  One lymph node Resident  DI TIAN  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Kevin Hughes MD Sharon Lisa Stein  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE LEFT AXILLA  EXCISION PART B  BREAST LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 13 10 CLINICAL DATA  An 84 year old female with biopsy proven infiltrating ductal carcinoma  underwent right modified radical mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  95   AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  5    GRADE REMOVED_DATE  EXTENDING TO WITHIN LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE CAUTERIZED INFERIOR MARGIN  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN FIFTEEN OF FIFTEEN LYMPH NODES  0 15   BIOPSY SITE AND FAT NECROSIS  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH MICROCYSTS  APOCRINE METAPLASIA  FIBROSIS  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  AND MICROCALCIFICATION IN BENIGN GLANDS   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The nipple is free of tumor  There are rare foci suspicious for lymphatic invasion  Focally  ductal carcinoma in situ extends well beyond the main tumor  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 37                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen with a skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 9 0cm  The entire specimen including the axillary tail and underlying breast parenchyma measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm  The nipple is 4 0cm from the superior margin and 5 0cm from the inferior margin of the skin ellipse  There is a healed horizontal incision in the medial half of the skin ellipse  which measures 3 0cm in length  The incision is 2 8cm from the superior skin margin  2 8cm from the inferior skin margin and 3 5cm from the medial margin  On sectioning through the breast parenchyma the tissue directly beneath the skin incision reveals a firm  yellow  well demarcated mass with an irregular border  The mass measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 6cm in dimension  Centrally there is a hemorrhagic region  measuring REMOVED_DATE in diameter  In addition  there are regions of yellow chalky  slightly firm fat between the mass and the overlying skin incision  The mass appears to abut the inferior inked margin  In addition  the mass is 0 3cm from the closest deep margin The tumor mass is 5 0cm from the superior margin  Sectioning through the remainder of the breast parenchyma reveals focal regions where there is increased white  rubbery fibrosis  No other nodules or firm areas are identified grossly  Multiple lymph nodes are identified within the axillary tail region  the largest of these measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm and the smallest measures 0 1cm in diameter  Section Code A E   tumor and inferior and deep margins F   medial superior quadrant G   medial inferior quadrant  near tumor H   lateral inferior quadrant I   lateral superior quadrant J   nipple K   biopsy site  skin L P   axillary tail lymph nodes Resident  C  Diana Jordan  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  WHITE 03 OPERATING ROOM REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  Peter Hedberg  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST TISSUE   report_end  , Unchecked.
