Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 13 CLINICAL DATA  74 year old lady with right breast cancer  Has had mastectomy on left side previously                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY AND AXILLARY DISSECTION  1  BIOPSY CAVITY WITH FAT NECROSIS  FIBROSIS  HEMORRHAGE AND GIANT CELL TYPE REACTION  2  HEALED INCISION SITE  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  INCLUDING FIBROSIS  MICROCYSTS AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA  4  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  5  THIRTY TWO OF THIRTY TWO AXILLARY LYMPH NODES ARE NEGATIVE FOR MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 19 12                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm modified radical mastectomy specimen which includes a REMOVED_DATE x 9 0cm skin ellipse with eccentrically located REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm areola with central 1 2cm nipple  There is a 2 0cm well healed scar located 4 0cm superolateral to the nipple and 1 5cm inferior to the closest inked superior margin  Just inferior to the nipple there is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm ecchyomosis  The specimen also includes a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail from which an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm aggregate of tan brown lymph nodes are dissected from the surrounding fibroadipose tissue  The deep surface of the specimen is smooth  glistening and unremarkable  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm biopsy cavity filled with maroon grumous material lying 1 5cm subadjacent to the old scar and 2 7cm from the closest deep inked margin  Sectioning through the remaining breast parenchyma reveals unremarkable fibroadipose tissue transversed by thick  fibrous bands  SECTION CODE  A J  lymph nodes  K  closest inked margin  deep   L O  representative cross section through biopsy cavity  P Q  representative suspicious medial areas  R  representative suspicious lateral areas  S  areola  T  scar  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST TISSUE  RIGHT    report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 47 CLINICAL DATA  The patient presents with a left breast lesion                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA WITH MICROCALCIFICATIONS  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 1 3   98   AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBRIFORM SOLID TYPE  2   SEE NOTE  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH CYSTS  FIBROSIS  AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA  NOTE  The infiltrating carcinoma is 2 0cm in greatest dimension  and focally extends to an inked margin of resection  The margin is free of carcinoma in situ  Vascular invasion is not identified  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Shane Meehan  MD Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 52                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with needle localization and accompanying roentgenogram  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a white  firm  stellate lesion that approaches the inked margin  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remainder of the specimen is submitted entirely in A through K  with the lesion in D through F  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  BREAST LEFT BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Robert James Boyd  M D  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST LESION   report_end  , Unchecked.
