 hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 09 05     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm fragment of cauterized  semifirm breast tissue  inked and sectioned to reveal fibrous breast parenchyma with multiple cysts measuring up to 0 3cm in diameter  The specimen is submitted in its entirety in cassettes A and B  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIANGOSIS  RIGHT BREAST   NO GROSS EVIDENCE OF INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  FLIEDER DOUGLAS  NO ADDRESS  O R  Diagnosis by  Asif Rashid  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS , Unchecked.
