ce measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm with a large REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm lymph node adjacent to a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm firm blue area  The specimen is bivalved and entirely frozen as FX  3  The specimen is entirely resubmitted in cassette C  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel hot and blue  are 2 blue lymph nodes measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  The larger node is bivalved and entirely frozen as FX  4  This node is entirely resubmitted in cassette D  The smaller node is frozen as FX  5  This node is entirely resubmitted in cassette E  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast lumpectomy  is a yellow lobulated REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm breast specimen  There is a short stitch marking the superior position and a long stitch marking the lateral position  The specimen is inked as follows  blue anterior  black posterior  The specimen was serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm stellate gritty mass which came to  0 2cm from the anterior margin  closest margin   This specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes F Q from medial to lateral  Please note the closest margin is in cassette M  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right mastectomy and axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm right mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE skin ellipse  The axillary tail measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm at one end of the specimen  The specimen is oriented by a long stitch marking lateral position and a short stitch marking the superior position  The external surface of the breast is inked in black and it is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm stellate nodule  nodule  1  with a central 0 1cm cavity  This cavity is 1 0cm superior to the nipple and 4 5cm lateral to the nipple  It comes to 1 2cm from the deep resection margin and 0 3cm from the anterior resection margin  There is also an irregular  rubbery  firm  stellate nodule  nodule  2  measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm in the middle portion of the specimen  Nodule  2 is 4 0cm inferior to the nipple and REMOVED_DATE lateral to the nipple and abuts the anterior resection margin  Another irregular rubbery firm nodule  nodule  3  can be found 5 0cm lateral to the nipple and 3 0cm inferior to it  This area measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm and is 1 5cm from the proximal resection margin  closest margin   The remainder of the breast consists of yellow white fatty fibrous tissue  Representative sections were submitted as follows  R  Closest margin to nodule  1 with portion of nodule  S T  Representative sections of nodule  1  U  Representative section of nodule   2 which is REMOVED_DATE inferior to the nipple including anterior resection margin  V W  Representative sections of breast close to nodule  2  X  Area of breast between nodule  2 and nodule  3  Y  Representative section of nodule  3 which is 3 0cm inferior to the nipple  NN  Nodule  1 Z  Anterior resection margin of nodule  3  AA  Posterior resection closest to nodule  3 BB  Area between nodule  2 and 3  CC  Normal appearing breast tissue away from these masses  medial end   DD  1 large bisected lymph node  EE II  Multiple lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  non sentinel lymph node right axilla  for permanent   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm lymph node with attached fat  This specimen is bisected and submitted in toto in cassette JJ  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shave margin left breast  are several fragments of yellow soft fatty tissue measuring in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  This specimen is submitted in toto in cassette