LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA IN SEVEN LYMPH NODES  0 7   SEE NOTE   NOTE  All the 7 negative lymph nodes show therapeutic effect  post neoadjuvant chemotherapy Sataloff Grading  N A   No lymphovascular invasion is present  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 2 containers which are both  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  Nelson  REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  left breast   is a 32 x 19 x 9cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen with a stitch designating the 12 o clock aspect  There is a 32 x 15cm portion of attached skin with a 1 5cm in diameter unremarkable nipple  The skin looks slightly thickened throughout and with a probable 3 4cm in length linear scar located in the lower outer portion of the breast  The anterior margin of the specimen is inked blue and the posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm tan yellow indurated tumor bed  mass  1   which is located in the upper outer quadrant  0 8cm from the closest posterior resection margin and 3cm from the closest anterior resection margin  Four other masses are identified  There is a 0 6cm nodule  mass  2  adjacent to mass  1  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm firm tan white nodule  mass  3  that is located 7cm lateral from the larger mass  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm firm tan white nodule  mass  4  located in the central lower aspect of the breast  10cm away from mass  1 and 7cm away from mass  3  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm well circumscribed tan white firm nodule  mass  5  which is also located in the central lower portion of the breast  19cm from mass  1  14cm from mass  3 and 9cm from mass  4  The remaining breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable and no other masses are identified  Upon examining the axillary tail  no lymph nodes are grossly appreciated  Sections of the specimen are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tumor bed  mass  1  entirely submitted   with the closest posterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass  2  adjacent to mass  1  entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the upper outer breast quadrant  including the parenchyma between mass  1 and mass  3   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass  3  entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the lower outer breast quadrant  including the parenchyma between mass  1 and mass  4   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass  4  entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the lower inner breast quadrant  including the parenchyma between mass  1 and mass  5   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass  5  entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of the upper inner breast quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the skin closest to mass  1   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the axillary tail tissue  Received fresh  labeled  left axillary contents   are multiple fragments of yellow tan soft tissue measuring in aggregate 8 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  Seven lymph nodes are identified ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 3 5cm in greatest dimension  The largest lymph node is indurated with a heterogeneously white  focal yellow and tan brown cut surface  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   A trisected lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   A bisected lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   4 lymph nodes  Final Diagnosis by Adriana Dionigi Corben M D   Electronically signed on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 16   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12 02 54PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 16   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02 37 07PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   2 RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  169  to chromosome 17 signals  134  in 60 t