 following manner  anterior blue  posterior black  medial green  lateral yellow  Serial sectioning through the specimens reveals areas of hemorrhage and fat necrosis lining the biopsy cavity  No tumor is grossly identified  Representative sections of lateral aspect of the biopsy cavity are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and representative sections of the medial biopsy cavity are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  re excision inferior half of cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm horseshoe shaped portion of tan brown fibroadipose tissue with a long stitch designating lateral and a short stitch designating inferior  The inside of the horseshoe is the biopsy cavity and shows focal areas of scarring and shaggy tissue  The biopsy cavity measures 0 8cm from the lateral resection margin  0 4cm from the inferior resection margin  0 5cm from the medial resection margin  and is continuous with the anterior  posterior and superior aspects of the specimen  which is inked with respect to the superior inferior long axis in the following manner  anterior blue  posterior black  medial green  lateral yellow  Serial sectioning reveals a tan yellow fatty cut surface with focal areas of fat necrosis and hemorrhage  Representative sections of the lateral aspect of the biopsy cavity are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and representative sections of the anteromedial aspect are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Matthew M Johnson M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Matthew M Johnson M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT  SUPERIOR HALF OF CAVITY MARGIN   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT  INFERIOR HALF OF CAVITY MARGIN  EXCISION , Unchecked.
